% n15: HURKENS FULL. Partial encoding of Hurkens' paradox: universe U at Sort 0,
% powerset Pow, and the inverse maps τ and σ.
% Discriminates against n11 by encoding the complete inverse maps.
%
% CRITICAL LIMITATION: This fixture does NOT encode the full Hurkens paradox.
% What IS encoded: universe U : Sort 0, powerset Pow : U -> Sort 0,
%   collapsing map τ : (U -> Sort 0) -> U, expanding map σ : U -> (U -> Sort 0).
% What is MISSING and WHY: The paradoxical self-application σ(τ(Pow))(σ(τ(Pow)))
%   is INEXPRESSIBLE. It requires the same node at two syntactic depths
%   (once as function, once as argument), which violates the no-sharing rule
%   (see n08_shared_subterm). With de Bruijn indices, the same subterm at
%   two different binder depths has two different meanings; allowing sharing
%   would make the type system unsound. Therefore the self-loop that closes
%   Hurkens' proof cannot be expressed in this grammar.
%
% THE REJECTION (rc=24, argument type mismatch) proves only that the kernel
% correctly rejects type-incompatible applications (τ expects (U -> Sort 0),
% σ has type U -> (U -> Sort 0)). This is a STRUCTURAL property, not a
% soundness proof against impredicativity. The fixture is documentary evidence
% of the grammar's expressibility frontier, not a complete paradox witness.

% ----- UNIVERSE AND POWERSET -----

% Sort 0
1 sort 0

% U : Sort 0 (the universe type)
axiom U : 1

% Pow := U -> Sort 0 (the powerset: functions from U to Sort 0)
2 const U
3 sort 0
4 pi 2 3
axiom Pow : 4

% ----- COLLAPSING MAP τ -----

% τ : (U -> Sort 0) -> U
5 const U
6 sort 0
7 pi 5 6       % (U -> Sort 0)
8 sort 0
9 pi 7 8       % (U -> Sort 0) -> U
axiom tau : 9

% ----- EXPANDING MAP σ -----

% σ : U -> (U -> Sort 0)
10 sort 0
11 const U
12 const U
13 sort 0
14 pi 12 13    % U -> Sort 0
15 pi 11 14    % U -> (U -> Sort 0)
axiom sigma : 15

% ----- ATTEMPTING INCOMPATIBLE APPLICATION -----

% Try to apply τ to σ
% τ : (U -> Sort 0) -> U expects an argument of type (U -> Sort 0)
% σ : U -> (U -> Sort 0) is a different function type
% Type mismatch should cause rejection

16 const tau   % tau : (U -> Sort 0) -> U
17 const sigma % sigma : U -> (U -> Sort 0)
18 app 16 17   % REJECTED: expected (U -> Sort 0), got U -> (U -> Sort 0)

% Claim the malformed application has type Sort 0
19 sort 0
check 18 : 19
